// A logic function is total and has no precondition. Here the measure dropped
// only under `requires(n > 0)`, which the self call `bad(0)` breaks and which
// nothing checks, so the definitional axiom `bad(n) == bad(0) + 1` was false at
// n = 0 and proved `r == 42` for a program that returns 7
// (issues/fixed/2026-11-27-a-recursive-ghost-fn-axiom-is-inconsistent.md). The
// evaluator rejects the clause (E0930); valid/ghost-fn-recursive.yo guards its
// body with `cond(...)` instead.
pragma(Pragma.Verify);

bad :: ghost_fn(
  (fn(n : u8, requires(n > u8(0)), decreases(n)) -> u32)(bad(u8(0)) + u32(1))
);

wrong :: (fn(x : i32, requires(bad(u8(0)) == bad(u8(0))), ensures(r == i32(42))) -> (r : i32))(x);
